====================================================================================================
v91  QN-SPSA vs QLTO V6, swept on the same protocol TUNED was derived with
====================================================================================================
  Gacon, Zoufal, Carleo, Woerner, Quantum 5, 567 (2021), arXiv:2103.09232,
  implemented in Application/qnspsa.py.

  WHY THIS METHOD AND NOT ANOTHER. QN-SPSA is the only published method that
  matches V6's cost scaling - constant circuits per step, independent of M - AND
  carries the metric preconditioning that beats V6 on MaxCut N=6, where full QNG
  reaches 0.0047 against V6's 0.0904 for 52x the circuits. If QNG-quality
  geometry is available at constant cost, V6's niche is smaller than the 8-problem
  suite suggests. That is the question this answers.

  IMPLEMENTATION VERIFIED BEFORE USE. The QFIM point-estimate was checked against
  the exactly computed Fubini-Study metric, averaged over 4000 samples with exact
  fidelities:

      N=2 reps=1 M=8   correlation +0.99502   scale 0.98523
      N=3 reps=1 M=12  correlation +0.99255   scale 0.96166

  Positive correlation confirms the leading -1/2 in the point estimate; without
  it the update ASCENDS and would read as a tuning failure. Scale near 1 confirms
  the 1/(2 eps^2) factor.

  COST. The paper counts 6 function evaluations per step. On a Pauli sum that is
  not 6 circuits: the 2 loss evaluations need one circuit per commuting group,
  while the 4 fidelity evaluations are compute-uncompute circuits measured once
  in the computational basis and cost one each. Billed as 2G + 4 plus blocking's
  loss checks - measured 7.1/step at MaxCut (G=1) and 13.3/step at Heisenberg
  (G=3), against V6's 1 and 3.

